<title>INDIA: India Oriental Bank 96/97 1st half up.</title>
<headline>India Oriental Bank 96/97 1st half up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Interest earned	   6,140.7  vs  4,629.0</p>
<p>    Other income		  510.7  vs    478.7</p>
<p>    Total income		6,651.4  vs  5,107.7</p>
<p>    Interest expended	 3,999.5  vs  2,780.7</p>
<p>    Operating expenses	1,104.2  vs  1,048.0</p>
<p>    Total expenditure	 5,103.7  vs  3,828.7</p>
<p>    Profit			1,547.7  vs  1,279.0</p>
<p>Note: State-run Oriental Bank of Commerce said the profit figure was arrived at after providing for interest tax of 97 million rupees against 70 million a year ago but before income tax, bonus, gratuity and impact of provisioning due to asset clarification. These adjustments would be made at the year-end.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
</text>
